findings.comment:
750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) walkin cooler shelves (mold);
B) sprayer - crevice around surface where water comes out (mold/buildup);
C) dish machine - plastic curtain on dirty side (mold/buildup); 
D) hot holding drawers on server line (splash/buildup on inner brackets);  and
E) metal pan at bar holding mixers by 3 part sink (splash/buildup).

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) soda gun holder at bar (buildup in the bottom) - cleaned and sanitized during inspection;
B) can opener - blade & crevice around blade (grimy buildup & metal shavings);
C) pan in bread hot holding drawer (puddling moisture with white coloration) - taken to dish area for ware washing;
D) slicer - non-removable parts (food debris); 
E) inside large ice machine - side walls and left corner of baffle (mold);   and
F) knife on cook line from previous evening (food debris) - taken to dish area to go through ware washing.

Clean and sanitize food contact between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.
